.SH DESCRIPTION
The product does not implement or incorrectly implements one or more security\-relevant checks as specified by the design of a standardized algorithm, protocol, or technique.
.SH KNOWN EXPLOITED VULNERABILITIES
CISA KEV catalog (as of 2026-11-15): \fB1\fR exploited CVE mapped to this weakness. Each entry has the catalog write\-up of how it was used in the wild (not a runnable exploit) and the required remediation. Code\-level vulnerable\->fixed pairs, when curated, are under \fBEXAMPLES\fR.
.SS CVE\-2024\-7965
Google Chromium V8, added 2024\-08\-28.
.PP
Google Chromium V8 Inappropriate Implementation Vulnerability.
.PP
\fIHow it is exploited (CISA):\fR
Google Chromium V8 contains an inappropriate implementation vulnerability that allows a remote attacker to potentially exploit heap corruption via a crafted HTML page. This vulnerability could affect multiple web browsers that utilize Chromium, including, but not limited to, Google Chrome, Microsoft Edge, and Opera.
.PP
\fIRemediation:\fR
Apply mitigations per vendor instructions, or discontinue use.
 Due 2024\-09\-18.
.PP
